From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:18:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] security/tpm: Start the log before vboot's first measurement

The log of measured boot is started, with the measurements of the CRTM
(the FMAP, the bootblock) and, in the bootblock, by clearing the pre-RAM
log, at the first CBFS measurement. With vboot starting in the
bootblock, verstage extends vboot's PCRs (boot mode, HWID, firmware
version) before that: their entries go into a pre-RAM log that nothing
has set up, as the cache-as-RAM came up. In QEMU, where it reads zeros,
each is dropped ("TPM LOG: log table is full") although the PCR is
extended, so the log no longer replays to the PCR; on real cache-as-RAM
the header is whatever the cache held.

Start the log, once, at the first measurement of any kind:
tspi_crtm_init_once(), which tspi_cbfs_measurement_banks() and
tpm_extend_pcr_banks() call. The CRTM measurements then come first in
the log, before vboot's.

TEST=QEMU q35 with vboot A/B, a TPM 2.0 (swtpm), TPM_MEASURED_BOOT: the
log starts with the FMAP and the bootblock, then vboot's three PCR 1
measurements, no "log table is full".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/security/tpm/tspi/crtm.c | 28 +++++++++++++++++++---------
 src/security/tpm/tspi/crtm.h |  7 +++++++
 src/security/tpm/tspi/tspi.c | 11 +++++++++++
 3 files changed, 37 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/security/tpm/tspi/crtm.c b/src/security/tpm/tspi/crtm.c
index 14abd0cea9..629d73bb51 100644
--- a/src/security/tpm/tspi/crtm.c
+++ b/src/security/tpm/tspi/crtm.c
@@ -125,6 +125,22 @@ static bool is_runtime_data(const char *name)
 	return !strcmp(allowlist, name);
 }
 
+tpm_result_t tspi_crtm_init_once(void)
+{
+	tpm_result_t rc;
+
+	if (tpm_log_available())
+		return TPM_SUCCESS;
+
+	rc = tspi_init_crtm();
+	if (rc) {
+		printk(BIOS_WARNING, "Initializing CRTM failed!\n");
+		return rc;
+	}
+	printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "CRTM initialized.\n");
+	return TPM_SUCCESS;
+}
+
 tpm_result_t tspi_cbfs_measurement(const char *name, uint32_t type, const struct vb2_hash *hash)
 {
 	return tspi_cbfs_measurement_banks(name, type, hash, NULL);
@@ -138,15 +154,9 @@ tpm_result_t tspi_cbfs_measurement_banks(const char *name, uint32_t type,
 	tpm_result_t rc = TPM_SUCCESS;
 	char tpm_log_metadata[TPM_CB_LOG_PCR_HASH_NAME];
 
-	if (!tpm_log_available()) {
-		rc = tspi_init_crtm();
-		if (rc) {
-			printk(BIOS_WARNING,
-			       "Initializing CRTM failed!\n");
-			return rc;
-		}
-		printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "CRTM initialized.\n");
-	}
+	rc = tspi_crtm_init_once();
+	if (rc)
+		return rc;
 
 	switch (type) {
 	case CBFS_TYPE_MRC_CACHE:
diff --git a/src/security/tpm/tspi/crtm.h b/src/security/tpm/tspi/crtm.h
index d1065ff783..84e4fe32da 100644
--- a/src/security/tpm/tspi/crtm.h
+++ b/src/security/tpm/tspi/crtm.h
@@ -46,6 +46,13 @@ tpm_result_t tspi_measure_cache_to_pcr(void);
  */
 tpm_result_t tspi_cbfs_measurement(const char *name, uint32_t type, const struct vb2_hash *hash);
 
+/**
+ * Start the log (the pre-RAM one in the bootblock) with the measurements of
+ * the CRTM, unless done already. Every measurement does it first, so that
+ * the first one, a CBFS file or vboot's boot mode, is logged after them.
+ */
+tpm_result_t tspi_crtm_init_once(void);
+
 /**
  * tspi_cbfs_measurement() with also the SHA-1 digest of the file, for
  * TPM_MEASURED_BOOT_SHA1_BANK (NULL: the main bank only).
diff --git a/src/security/tpm/tspi/tspi.c b/src/security/tpm/tspi/tspi.c
index 0f2ec34c89..fa4227b85e 100644
--- a/src/security/tpm/tspi/tspi.c
+++ b/src/security/tpm/tspi/tspi.c
@@ -234,6 +234,17 @@ tpm_result_t tpm_extend_pcr_banks(int pcr, enum vb2_hash_algorithm digest_algo,
 	if (!digest)
 		return TPM_IOERROR;
 
+	/*
+	 * vboot extends its PCRs in verstage before any CBFS measurement: the
+	 * log must be started first, or the pre-RAM log is still as the
+	 * cache-as-RAM came up and the entry is lost.
+	 */
+	if (CONFIG(TPM_MEASURED_BOOT)) {
+		rc = tspi_crtm_init_once();
+		if (rc)
+			return rc;
+	}
+
 	if (tspi_tpm_is_setup()) {
 		rc = tlcl_lib_init();
 		if (rc != TPM_SUCCESS) {
-- 
